import "../../../../sass/accessibility.scss";
import { urls } from "../../../../data";

<div class="a11y-pattern-content">
  <h1>Filter Input Accessibility</h1>
  <h2>Best Practices</h2>
  <p>
    A filter input is a plain textbox, not a
    <a href=`${urls.components}/combobox`>combobox</a> . Its results are
    <strong>not</strong> intended to appear in a popup listbox, so combobox ARIA
    ( <code>role="combobox"</code> , <code>aria-expanded</code> ,
    <code>aria-activedescendant</code> ) does not apply. If you need a popup of
    suggestions, use combobox instead.
  </p>
  <p>
    The input typically relies on placeholder text (e.g. "Filter") rather than a
    visible <code>&lt;label&gt;</code> . Placeholder text is not a substitute
    for a label — always provide an accessible name via <code>aria-label</code>
    that describes what is being filtered (e.g. "Filter results").
  </p>
  <p>
    The input <strong>must</strong> use <code>aria-controls</code> to reference
    the <code>id</code> of the content it filters, so assistive technology can
    discover the relationship even though that content isn't a popup the input
    expands or collapses.
  </p>
  <p>
    If filtering updates a count or list of results elsewhere on the page, that
    update <strong>must</strong> be announced without moving focus from the
    input. Use a
    <a href=`${urls.accessibility}/techniques/live-region`>live region</a> for
    this, and keep the announcement short (e.g. "12 results") rather than
    reading back the entire filtered list.
  </p>
  <p>
    The clear button, when present, has no visible text and
    <strong>must</strong> have an <code>aria-label</code> describing its action
    (e.g. "Clear filter input"). The search icon is decorative and
    <strong>must</strong> use <code>aria-hidden="true"</code> .
  </p>
  <h2>Interaction Design</h2>
  <p>
    This section provides detailed instructions for how different input types
    should navigate and operate the pattern.
  </p>
  <h3>Keyboard</h3>
  <p>
    Pressing <strong>TAB</strong> key <strong>must</strong> move focus to the
    input. Typing filters the associated content live, without requiring
    <strong>ENTER</strong>.
  </p>
  <p>
    When a clear button is rendered, <strong>TAB</strong> key
    <strong>must</strong> move focus to it next, and pressing
    <strong>ENTER</strong> or <strong>SPACEBAR</strong><strong>must</strong>
    activate it, clearing the input's value.
  </p>
  <p>
    Unlike combobox or listbox patterns, arrow keys have no special behavior
    here — they move the text cursor within the input as normal.
  </p>
  <h3>Screen Reader</h3>
  <p>
    A screen reader announces the input's accessible name, its role ("search"
    text field, due to the underlying <code>type="search"</code> ), and its
    current value.
  </p>
  <p>When focus moves to the clear button, its label is announced.</p>
  <p>
    Typing into the input does <strong>not</strong> automatically announce the
    filtered results — this must be wired up separately via a live region on the
    element referenced by <code>aria-controls</code> .
  </p>
  <h3>Pointer</h3>
  <p>
    Clicking or tapping the input <strong>must</strong> place focus in it.
    Clicking or tapping the clear button <strong>must</strong> clear the input's
    value.
  </p>
  <h2>ARIA Reference</h2>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Attribute</th>
        <th>Description</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>type="search"</strong></td>
        <td>
          Changes the input's role to "searchbox" and gives mobile browsers a
          reason to show a search-optimized virtual keyboard.
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>aria-label</strong></td>
        <td>
          Provides the accessible name for the input, since a visible label is
          typically not used. Also provides the clear button with an accessible
          name, since it has no visible text.
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>aria-controls</strong></td>
        <td>
          References the <code>id</code> of the content that this input filters.
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>aria-hidden="true"</strong></td>
        <td>
          Applied to the decorative search icon inside the input to hide it from
          assistive technology.
        </td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <h2>Further Reading</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <a href=`${urls.accessibility}/techniques/live-region`>Live Region</a>
    </li>
    <li><a href=`${urls.components}/textbox`>Textbox</a></li>
    <li><a href=`${urls.components}/combobox`>Combobox</a></li>
  </ul>
</div>
